# Representations determined by characters in characteristic 0
%%%
tag := "Chapter4/Corollary4.2.4"
number := false
%%%

**Corollary 4.2.4.** _Any finite dimensional representation of $`G` is determined by its character if $`k` has characteristic $`0`; namely, $`\chi_V = \chi_W` implies $`V \cong W`._

